---
/**
 * Leagues — the retention engine, and the worst-executed page type in the
 * corpus. Ported to the converged Paper design 2026-08-03 (FW-3967);
 * spec in `design/SUBPAGE-EXPLORATION.md`.
 *
 * **The idea: the season is a TRACK, not a catalogue.** In August both venues
 * are between seasons, so a page built as a list of leagues you can join is a
 * page whose every row says "no". A track says something true and useful
 * instead — here is where the season is, and here is when the thing you want
 * happens. That is why `SeasonTrack` sits in the hero-strip position: it is the
 * ONE justified exception to the 4-cell strip, same furniture, but its rule is
 * only partly filled because progress is the fact it exists to show.
 *
 * **The capture band is the largest thing after the hero**, deliberately. Across
 * all 126 audited simulator and golf-course sites, exactly ZERO offered a
 * waitlist, while 11% of league pages say "registration closed" and simply stop
 * (playbook-core.md §5). The one component nobody else has should not be a
 * footnote. (126 is the WHOLE audit — sim venues plus golf courses; the 96 in
 * `data/global.ts` is the sim-venue subset. Always name which. And keep the
 * comparison internal: it is a competitive claim about named third parties and
 * belongs in comments, never in copy a customer reads.)
 *
 * **The band is also this page's one ember field.** SUBPAGE-EXPLORATION §"Paper
 * quirks" flags that ember goes unused on dark-heavy pages, because every CTA on
 * a dark block inverts to an amber fill. A page that never shows the brand's
 * action colour is worth avoiding, so the capture band is ember at full strength
 * — once, like the homepage's.
 *
 * **"On the blanks" is the page's closing note and it is a promise, not an
 * apology.** Four facts are unpublished for both venues; the note commits to
 * publishing night, format, length and price TOGETHER, before registration
 * opens rather than after you have paid. Nobody asked for that. It turns the
 * page's largest gap into the reason to trust it, and it is the single idea from
 * this page's exploration most worth keeping.
 */
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import LeagueBlock from '../components/venue/LeagueBlock.astro';
import LeagueSchema from '../components/venue/LeagueSchema.astro';
import SeasonTrack from '../components/venue/SeasonTrack.astro';
import SectionHead from '../components/venue/SectionHead.astro';
import WaitlistForm from '../components/venue/WaitlistForm.astro';

const leagues = (await getCollection('leagues'))
  .filter((l) => l.data.published)
  .sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order);

const season = leagues[0]?.data.season ?? 'the coming season';

const metadata = {
  metaTitle: 'Indoor Golf Leagues — Lakeville & Stillwater, MN',
  metaDescription:
    'Fall and winter simulator golf leagues at The Links, Lakeville and Stillwater MN. Handicapped and beginner-friendly. Join the list for the next season.',
};

/**
 * The three steps of a season, in order over time — the site's ONE sanctioned
 * use of the `01 / 02 / 03` numerals after convergence. `activeIndex` is 0
 * because both venues are between seasons today; move it when the lineup lands
 * and the filled rule moves with it.
 */
const steps = [
  {
    marker: 'Now',
    title: 'Between seasons',
    body: 'Summer play has wound down. There is nothing to register for yet, and we are not going to pretend otherwise.',
  },
  {
    marker: 'Next',
    title: 'The lineup is published',
    body: 'Night, format, length and price — all four at once, so you can decide with the whole picture in front of you.',
  },
  {
    marker: 'Then',
    title: 'Registration opens',
    body: 'Everyone on the list hears the day it does. Teams fill fastest in the first week.',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout metadata={metadata}>
  {
    /* 1. HERO — midnight, venue-neutral. The season is named in the eyebrow
      because "which season is this page about" is the first question a returning
      player has, and half the corpus never answers it. */
  }
  <section class="on-dark bg-midnight">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-content px-gutter pt-s8 pb-s7 lg:px-gutter-lg lg:pt-s9 lg:pb-s8">
      <p class="caps-label text-amber">{season}</p>
      <h1 class="mt-s5 text-hero leading-hero font-extrabold tracking-display-tight text-white">Leagues</h1>
      <p class="mt-s5 max-w-prose-page border-l-slab border-amber pl-s4 text-lead leading-body text-paper">
        The cheapest way to play all winter, and the fastest way to meet people who also think Tuesday is a golf night.
        Handicaps keep matches fair, so a first-timer and a scratch player can be on the same team.
      </p>

      {
        /* 2. THE SEASON TRACK, in the hero-strip position. The justified
          exception — see the file header and `SeasonTrack`. */
      }
      <SeasonTrack class="mt-s8" steps={steps} activeIndex={0} tone="dark" />
    </div>
  </section>

  {
    /* 3. THE CAPTURE BAND. The largest thing after the hero, and the page's one
      ember field at full strength.

      Nothing dark goes on this band: midnight on ember is 2.35:1 and navy
      1.79:1 — the same measurement that forbids an ember fill on the hero, read
      the other way round. The form therefore sits in a paper slab punched out of
      the band, and inside that slab everything reverts to light-field styling. */
  }
  <section class="on-accent-band bg-primary">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-content px-gutter py-section lg:px-gutter-lg lg:py-section-lg">
      <div class="grid gap-s7 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:items-start lg:gap-s9">
        <div>
          <p class="caps-label text-white">Before anyone else</p>
          <h2 class="mt-s4 text-section leading-display font-extrabold tracking-display-tight text-white">
            Get first word on {season}
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-s5 text-lead leading-body text-surface">
            Registration has not opened at either venue. One email the day it does — that is the whole arrangement, and
            it is the only mail you will get from us.
          </p>
          <p
            class="my-s6 border-y-score border-white py-s4 font-display text-row leading-display font-bold tracking-display text-white"
          >
            Teams fill fastest in the first week. The list is how you are in it.
          </p>
        </div>

        <WaitlistForm
          listName="league-general"
          heading="Join the list"
          blurb="One email when registration opens. Nothing else, ever."
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 4. THE VENUE BLOCKS — one ruled column, not two cards. */}
  <section class="bg-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-content px-gutter py-section lg:px-gutter-lg lg:py-section-lg">
      <SectionHead index={1}>League play at both venues</SectionHead>
      {leagues.map((league, i) => <LeagueBlock league={league} first={i === 0} last={i === leagues.length - 1} />)}
    </div>
  </section>

  {
    /* 5. ON THE BLANKS. The closing note, and a commitment rather than a
      disclaimer. It is on greige so it reads as the page's own aside — and note
      that emberMid is 3.66:1 on greige (`rules.noWarningOnGreige`), which is why
      nothing here is set in the caution colour. */
  }
  <section class="bg-greige">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-content px-gutter py-section lg:px-gutter-lg lg:py-section-lg">
      <SectionHead index={2}>On the blanks</SectionHead>
      <div class="max-w-prose-page">
        <p class="text-lead leading-body text-inkBody">
          You will have noticed how much of the season above is not filled in. Night, format, length and price are not
          set for either venue yet, and we would rather show you the shape of the question than a number we would have
          to take back.
        </p>
        <p
          class="mt-s5 border-l-slab border-ember pl-s4 font-display text-card leading-display font-bold tracking-display text-ink"
        >
          When they are set, we will publish all four together — before registration opens, not after you have paid.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-s5 text-body leading-body text-inkBody">
          If a league night has to change once it is running, everyone playing hears it from us first.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <LeagueSchema leagues={leagues} />
</BaseLayout>
